// Fixture (expected-noop case): inherits BOTH branches of the diamond,
// each of which inherits the same base -- the base is reachable via two
// distinct paths. Both branches add nothing of their own. Must be
// recognized as a no-op: the resolved (name -> function_t*) comparison
// must dedupe the base's functions across both paths rather than
// spuriously treating the second path as "extra" content.
inherit "/clone/replace_program/replace_diamond_a";
inherit "/clone/replace_program/replace_diamond_b";
void create() { replace_program("/clone/replace_program/replace_min_target"); }
